{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown","id":142180,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion: Renown","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-19T02:08:17-07:00","id":142180,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion: Renown","content":"I don't know about you, but the forum is running very slowly for me as I post this. (Maybe it has the Resigned Condition? *dodges thrown projectiles*)<br /> <br /> Anyway, Renown won out (<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/renown/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/renown/</a>) and here's the place to talk about it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 05-19-2014, 05:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T03:35:19-07:00","id":142216,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">At last Renown feel as \u201cepic story points\u201d as it should be. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-includes/images/smilies/icon_smile.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> Nice touches.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Another question I think should be addressed \u2013 would Renown somehow let player collect extra Beats for playing it?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T03:49:49-07:00","id":142218,"title":"","content":"I love it. As I already said in the blog, I like the gambling aspect of flashing Renown around. At last it does something besides being a costly dice adder and power cap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T04:27:04-07:00","id":142226,"title":"","content":"Holy crap those inflicted conditions are powerful... And flaring renown feels like bating someone into a trap. &quot;Here, take +2; I'm gonna take 4 automatic successes, thank you very much.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T05:33:16-07:00","id":142239,"title":"","content":"Yep, even with 1 dot of Renown is totally worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T08:22:36-07:00","id":142321,"title":"","content":"I like it in general... But there is one thing I don't like: That you have to be challenged on what you try to project for it to be useful.<br /> <br /> This makes a tight-knit, well-working pack WEAKER than a dysfunctional one that bickers and questions each others motives and plans.<br /> <br /> I like the bonus to &quot;abuse&quot; someone's personality when they channel their Renown, and I also love the bonus... But I don't like that you'd have to be challenged for you to get any benefit from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T08:33:01-07:00","id":142328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=142321#post142321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it in general... But there is one thing I don't like: That you have to be challenged on what you try to project for it to be useful.<br /> <br /> This makes a tight-knit, well-working pack WEAKER than a dysfunctional one that bickers and questions each others motives and plans.<br /> <br /> I like the bonus to &quot;abuse&quot; someone's personality when they channel their Renown, and I also love the bonus... But I don't like that you'd have to be challenged for you to get any benefit from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A) Who says it's a member of the pack challenging them?<br /> <br /> B) I don't see how the Wisdom Condition would lead to a dysfunctional pack, not hardly unless the Ithateur has his head up his ass. Constructive criticism is a Good Thing (tm).<br /> <br /> C) Honor is a bit more valid but: &quot;Hey Mike, I've been meaning to call in that favor to not pay rent for this month...&quot; &quot;...Oh <i>all right, </i>you get to not be kicked out.&quot; &quot;Yay!&quot;<br /> <br /> D) A pack of wolves is a family. Living without arguments is not only a fool's errand, it's usually a sign of deeper issues (*cough*Pure brainwashing*hack*). You see a bug, I see a feature.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T08:33:56-07:00","id":142329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=142321#post142321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it in general... But there is one thing I don't like: That you have to be challenged on what you try to project for it to be useful. This makes a tight-knit, well-working pack WEAKER than a dysfunctional one that bickers and questions each others motives and plans. I like the bonus to &amp;quot;abuse&amp;quot; someone's personality when they channel their Renown, and I also love the bonus... But I don't like that you'd have to be challenged for you to get any benefit from it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Luckily that's an easy house rule to fix - you gain the free successes when you first flare your Renown and then gain the Condition after instead of the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T08:42:23-07:00","id":142335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=142321#post142321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it in general... But there is one thing I don't like: That you have to be challenged on what you try to project for it to be useful.<br /> <br /> This makes a tight-knit, well-working pack WEAKER than a dysfunctional one that bickers and questions each others motives and plans.<br /> <br /> I like the bonus to &quot;abuse&quot; someone's personality when they channel their Renown, and I also love the bonus... But I don't like that you'd have to be challenged for you to get any benefit from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, this is addressed in the test. The idea is to let the person shine. They flare their renown, and you're socially expected to step up and challenge. This isn't serious or life-threatening; this reaffirms their honor and dedication. So you're doing them a favor. Then they come back hardcore, and look badass for it. <br /> <br /> For a pack, this means your buddies act like straw men you can tear down to exalt your position. Like teamwork through adversity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T08:46:23-07:00","id":142336,"title":"","content":"Holy carpfish this is what Renown needed. What an improvement!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T08:55:04-07:00","id":142351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=142335#post142335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For what it's worth, this is addressed in the test. The idea is to let the person shine. They flare their renown, and you're socially expected to step up and challenge. This isn't serious or life-threatening; this reaffirms their honor and dedication. So you're doing them a favor. Then they come back hardcore, and look badass for it.<br /> <br /> For a pack, this means your buddies act like straw men you can tear down to exalt your position. Like teamwork through adversity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the element of social ritual this takes on, when described this way. Almost like a call-and-response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T08:58:02-07:00","id":142354,"title":"","content":"The thing for me on the Renown conditions is that it not being engaged is also a huge benefit.<br /> <br /> Think about it. The thing we're looking at right now is getting successes from someone challenging your renown, so what happens when no one challenges you?<br /> <br /> Easy- <i>No one dares challenge you.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T09:01:04-07:00","id":142356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=142321#post142321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it in general... But there is one thing I don't like: That you have to be challenged on what you try to project for it to be useful.<br /> <br /> This makes a tight-knit, well-working pack WEAKER than a dysfunctional one that bickers and questions each others motives and plans.<br /> <br /> I like the bonus to &quot;abuse&quot; someone's personality when they channel their Renown, and I also love the bonus... But I don't like that you'd have to be challenged for you to get any benefit from it.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Picture an Irraka challenging his Ithaeur\u2019s concerning the reseach of a spirit\u2019s ban/bane, merely to give himself +2 on his own attempt, and +X suxx on his own efforts, which would likely make his roll an exceptional success, which in turn would allow him to finish the task unbelievably fast.<br /> <br /> All of the above in a teamwork effort.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T09:43:33-07:00","id":142425,"title":"","content":"This also opens the way for a more Ragabash-like role in the pack (possibly shouldered largely by the irraka but not necessarily). Maybe there's one particular wolf whose job it is to (Semi-ritualistically) give everyone else a ration of shit to keep them sharp. Until it's their turn and literally everyone in the pack gives it right back to them. <br /> <br /> I dunno, this dynamic makes me happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T09:44:15-07:00","id":142429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=142335#post142335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For what it's worth, this is addressed in the test. The idea is to let the person shine. They flare their renown, and you're socially expected to step up and challenge. This isn't serious or life-threatening; this reaffirms their honor and dedication. So you're doing them a favor. Then they come back hardcore, and look badass for it.<br /> <br /> For a pack, this means your buddies act like straw men you can tear down to exalt your position. Like teamwork through adversity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Now it makes kinda sense. It's a bit strange to me still, but I think I can get used to it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T10:13:44-07:00","id":142452,"title":"","content":"The Wise thing makes sense to me. It's akin to having a speaker get up on the platform and give a talk. At the end, there's a Q&amp;A, not just for clarification, but for voicing disagreement and problems noticed during the talk. But the Wise listens to these and responds to them, either acknowledging the problems or explaining how they're not really problems. Putting yourself out there naturally invites more critical analysis.<br /> <br /> ...or a blog thread. /cough<br /> <br /> The most obvious situation I could see for this is having each member of an investigative team flaring brands and giving a pep talk shortly before actually digging in. A smattering of peer review and bonuses all around for the actual info-hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T10:42:17-07:00","id":142469,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if its intended this way, but the wise flare is particulary useful when the pack discuss what they know about the matter at hand. Consider this scenario: the pack is arguing or debating about what they know about a particular threat. The Itheur flares his wisdom and rolls first telling everyone what he knows about the subject in hand. Every other pack member can there try to challenge his knowledge, rolling with a plus 2, thus getting aditional information about the current issue. Finally the itheaur ponders about everything that has been said, looking for more information with some free succeses to make add to this roll.<br /> <br /> That whole setup might be extremely usefull and im not if its intended or is exploiting the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T11:37:21-07:00","id":142567,"title":"","content":"On the ragabash concept, I think you'll find that in a contrarian faceted iron master. My brother plays an irraka iron master with that facet. Gods is he a pain in the ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T12:46:28-07:00","id":142610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=142469#post142469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if its intended this way, but the wise flare is particulary useful when the pack discuss what they know about the matter at hand. Consider this scenario: the pack is arguing or debating about what they know about a particular threat. The Itheur flares his wisdom and rolls first telling everyone what he knows about the subject in hand. Every other pack member can there try to challenge his knowledge, rolling with a plus 2, thus getting aditional information about the current issue. Finally the itheaur ponders about everything that has been said, looking for more information with some free succeses to make add to this roll. That whole setup might be extremely usefull and im not if its intended or is exploiting the system.</div> </div> </div> </div> Would they all get the bonus, or would the first person to challenge the the Ithaeur &quot;break&quot; the Wise Condition and cause it to Resolve before the rest of the pack can take advantage of it? Either way, as ST I would call for a single teamwork roll in that situation rather than having everyone roll individually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T12:50:52-07:00","id":142612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=142610#post142610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Would they all get the bonus, or would the first person to challenge the the Ithaeur &quot;break&quot; the Wise Condition and cause it to Resolve before the rest of the pack can take advantage of it? Either way, as ST I would call for a single teamwork roll in that situation rather than having everyone roll individually.</div> </div> </div> </div>As currently writte, the condition ends when the werewolf wants to and at least one person has used the benefit, so anybody can use it until the werewolf uses the bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T13:02:43-07:00","id":142621,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of making Renown have increased and useful functionality, the way it works feels a bit clunky to me without seeing it used in play. Probably because I'm reading both Demon and Strix Chronicle right now and keep jumping around from book to book, a bit of processor bottleneck has built up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T13:18:02-07:00","id":142632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quimeradc</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=142612#post142612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As currently writte, the condition ends when the werewolf wants to and at least one person has used the benefit, so anybody can use it until the werewolf uses the bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's how I read it as well, I just wanted a second opinion. I stand by my previous post though, if I'm ST and my players attempt that, I would make it a single teamwork roll instead of a bunch of separate attempts. Each roll would still get the +2, but my rule of thumb is that when more than one player in the same party attempts the same action in the same scene, it's done as teamwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T13:30:25-07:00","id":142638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=142351#post142351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like the element of social ritual this takes on, when described this way. Almost like a call-and-response.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's about what I was thinking too. I'm really excited about this as it will give my players a lot more reason to A. actually take renown seriously in play and B. Have more reasons to roleplay how a werewolf should/can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T23:00:43-07:00","id":143127,"title":"","content":"I'm glad that Renown's actually useful now, and werewolves will actually want to play up their Renown. When my players first saw Renown in the WtF core, they thought it was just an XP sink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T23:01:49-07:00","id":143128,"title":"","content":"The image I kept getting whilst reading the renown challenge/response was a football team (and a lot of native peoples, but football is an easier explanation). In my few years playing football, it was common for players to call each other out and &quot;rip&quot; on each other, to encourage each other to play harder. The big, heavy hitting player not hitting hard enough? You called them a wuss (or worse) they'd smile and insult your mother, immediately before going on field and tearing someone's head off as a gesture of defiance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T23:18:22-07:00","id":143134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=143128#post143128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The image I kept getting whilst reading the renown challenge/response was a football team (and a lot of native peoples, but football is an easier explanation). In my few years playing football, it was common for players to call each other out and &quot;rip&quot; on each other, to encourage each other to play harder. The big, heavy hitting player not hitting hard enough? You called them a wuss (or worse) they'd smile and insult your mother, immediately before going on field and tearing someone's head off as a gesture of defiance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. This. Very much the dynamic intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T01:25:09-07:00","id":143187,"title":"","content":"I am not sure I understand the timing of those automatic successes.<br /> In my experience we rarely have more than one investigation roll in a scene, but to have someone question your reasoning your must have already done your roll, right? So you come into a scene, roll to investigate it, then someone gets a die bonus to question your roll*, and after that you sit on those extra successes for possibly a few sessions waiting for the next investigation roll to use them on**? Or do they apply retroactively to the investigation roll you already made? And can you still apply them if someone successfully questioned your knowledge?<br /> Is there a way to get rid of the extra diceroll that the 'question their knowledge' step seems to require? I generally like to keep the amount of dicerolling to a minimum.<br /> <br /> *how does that work, is there a system for it? PC vs PC opposed roll or static difficulty? Does the Renown flaring Were have to shut for the rest of the scene if their opponent wins the roll to question them, or what happens?<br /> **Admittedly hyperbole for effect, as that would require an asshole ST. But realistically it might be a few scene before it's time for the next investigation roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 05-20-2014, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T02:01:19-07:00","id":143200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=143187#post143187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience we rarely have more than one investigation roll in a scene, but to have someone question your reasoning your must have already done your roll, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way the Conditions are worded, someone needs to challenge you on it before you can get the benefits; yes. So an effective pack with upon stepping into a situation where the Wisdom heavy character is about to roll their Investigation will challenge them before the investigation starts so that they're sharp and focused to prove themselves on the roll (getting all those extra successes).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you come into a scene, roll to investigate it, then someone gets a die bonus to question your roll*, and after that you sit on those extra successes for possibly a few sessions waiting for the next investigation roll to use them on**? </div> </div> </div>You, the way it is phrased, could sit on them for a bit. But you have three Skills to pick from. If they challenge you based on an investigation you did, it doesn't mean you can only apply the bonus to Investigation rolls.<br /> <br /> For example, you do an Investigation roll, your pack mate challenges you for not digging deeper or looking for more clues, and then you channel the bonus successes to an Occult roll to figure out a hidden supernatural meaning behind the events you just investigated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or do they apply retroactively to the investigation roll you already made? </div> </div> </div>Don't seem to be written that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And can you still apply them if someone successfully questioned your knowledge? </div> </div> </div>The mechanics aren't written such that it matters if the challenge itself is successful or not. Just that it happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there a way to get rid of the extra diceroll that the 'question their knowledge' step seems to require? I generally like to keep the amount of dicerolling to a minimum. </div> </div> </div>I guess? There's no reason why you have to roll it that we've seen so far. Though the full final rules in the book might have more details on what the challenging roll looks like and means. Maybe David will shed some light on this for us?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T02:15:06-07:00","id":143207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=143200#post143200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way the Conditions are worded, someone needs to challenge you on it before you can get the benefits; yes. So an effective pack with upon stepping into a situation where the Wisdom heavy character is about to roll their Investigation will challenge them before the investigation starts so that they're sharp and focused to prove themselves on the roll (getting all those extra successes).</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a bit more sense. So the intention in how it would actually play out is:<br /> Players come into situation -&gt; ST calls for investigation roll -&gt; PC1 decides to flare their renown, asks others to give them a moment before rolling to describe analyzing the scene -&gt; PC2 steps up and questions PC1's knowledge (diceroll with as of yet unknown effect) -&gt; PCs do the actual investigation roll and PC1 gets renown in extra successes.<br /> That correct?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=143200#post143200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess? There's no reason why you have to roll it that we've seen so far. Though the full final rules in the book might have more details on what the challenging roll looks like and means. Maybe David will shed some light on this for us?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's hope for it. I am loath to roll for stuff that has no mechanical effect as that's normally better left to the realm of roleplaying. If the condition could just as well read 'a packmate must roleplay questioning the character's foundation of knowledge' then I don't see a reason to include the extra roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T04:25:52-07:00","id":143303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=143207#post143207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Let's hope for it. I am loath to roll for stuff that has no mechanical effect as that's normally better left to the realm of roleplaying. If the condition could just as well read 'a packmate must roleplay questioning the character's foundation of knowledge' then I don't see a reason to include the extra roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to roleplay it and not roll it, that's fine. But then again, remember that particularly boosted dice pools give the potential for Conditions, which could affect later scenes mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T05:52:45-07:00","id":143347,"title":"","content":"It might very well be one of those crunchy ways to make an awesome fluff suggestion - I think the value it brings to inter/intra-pack behavior, before you even think about opportunities interacting with the rest of the world, makes the idea worth whatever quibbling you might have to do with your ST to keep from abusing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":".  'worth' not 'with'! silly autocorrect. 05-20-2014, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T06:10:23-07:00","id":143354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=143303#post143303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want to roleplay it and not roll it, that's fine. But then again, remember that particularly boosted dice pools give the potential for Conditions, which could affect later scenes mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, if the only reason you roll the dice is because of the off-chance of getting a condition just feels... cheap. It's like a player rolling to tie their shoelaces because they hope to roll well enough to get the Inspired condition.<br /> I'd like if more If, for example, the packmate's challenge roll would have to succeed in order for the channeling Werewolf to get the extra successes (standard difficulty). Then at least there is a reason to roll and a consequence for failling the roll (i.e. your friend's ribbing failed to spurn you to greater heights of skill). Like how Sherlock needs Watson's comments and questions to work at full capacity, and how you can't just substitute anyone else for him(/her). (On the other hand, that might make Wisdom channeling too dependant on your packmates compared to others Renown Channels).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T07:46:17-07:00","id":143431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=143354#post143354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, if the only reason you roll the dice is because of the off-chance of getting a condition just feels... cheap. It's like a player rolling to tie their shoelaces because they hope to roll well enough to get the Inspired condition.<br /> I'd like if more If, for example, the packmate's challenge roll would have to succeed in order for the channeling Werewolf to get the extra successes (standard difficulty). Then at least there is a reason to roll and a consequence for failling the roll (i.e. your friend's ribbing failed to spurn you to greater heights of skill). Like how Sherlock needs Watson's comments and questions to work at full capacity, and how you can't just substitute anyone else for him(/her). (On the other hand, that might make Wisdom channeling too dependant on your packmates compared to others Renown Channels).</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience trying it that way, it felt too limiting at the table. <br /> <br /> YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T08:05:01-07:00","id":143464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=143431#post143431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my experience trying it that way, it felt too limiting at the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that. I'll try it at least once the way it's presented just to see how it goes in play. It's just that, as a rule, if something makes a player roll their dice and then they look at you with expectant eyes and go &quot;I rolled a success/failure, what happens?&quot;, and your answer in both cases is &quot;nothing, really&quot;, then I'd rather not roll to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T10:17:47-07:00","id":143657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/142180-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-renown?p=143464#post143464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see that. I'll try it at least once the way it's presented just to see how it goes in play. It's just that, as a rule, if something makes a player roll their dice and then they look at you with expectant eyes and go &quot;I rolled a success/failure, what happens?&quot;, and your answer in both cases is &quot;nothing, really&quot;, then I'd rather not roll to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really what success should be. Something should always happen. <br /> <br /> Failure's a little weak in the system as-is. It's always been, though. That's the reason for the Dramatic Failure upgrade option, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}